{"nodes": [{"id": "cyber_wellness_quest_milestones_phase_0_foundation", "label": "Phase 0 - Foundation", "file_type": "document", "rationale": "Shared design system plus content schema: shared-component audit, 5-realm per-band schema, band-select in the Atlas Gate, Phaser as a scoped lazy dependency, placeholder asset pipeline. Programmer half done.", "source_file": "Cyber_Wellness_Quest_Milestones.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "cyber_wellness_quest_milestones_phase_1_content_authoring", "label": "Phase 1 - Content Authoring", "file_type": "document", "rationale": "Realm content data per band per realm for all 5 realms, the Report & Block component, Bully Bog's digital-footprint and 'who would you tell' beats, the 5th pledge line, and the hardcoded-realm-count audit. Done.", "source_file": "Cyber_Wellness_Quest_Milestones.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "cyber_wellness_quest_milestones_phase_2_new_mechanics", "label": "Phase 2 - New Mechanics", "file_type": "document", "rationale": "Platformer, stepping-stone decision run, and Detective/Compare. All three built; every realm is now playable end-to-end for both bands.", "source_file": "Cyber_Wellness_Quest_Milestones.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "cyber_wellness_quest_milestones_phase_3_backgrounds", "label": "Phase 3 - Backgrounds", "file_type": "document", "rationale": "Scaling the existing 9 backgrounds. Realistic total is ~13-14 pieces, not 18 - it is one shared world regardless of band, plus the Traveler's Room as an unplanned 10th location.", "source_file": "Cyber_Wellness_Quest_Milestones.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "cyber_wellness_quest_milestones_phase_4_polish_accessibility_qa", "label": "Phase 4 - Polish, Accessibility, QA", "file_type": "document", "rationale": "Reduced-motion, focus/hit targets, text-equivalent instructions, keyboard coverage, retry-without-penalty. Pieces exist but nothing has been checked end-to-end as a pass.", "source_file": "Cyber_Wellness_Quest_Milestones.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "cyber_wellness_quest_milestones_phase_5_playtest_launch", "label": "Phase 5 - Playtest & Launch", "file_type": "document", "rationale": "At least one real pilot per band, classroom or holiday take-home, before wide rollout.", "source_file": "Cyber_Wellness_Quest_Milestones.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "cyber_wellness_quest_milestones_asset_pipeline", "label": "Asset Pipeline (Placeholders & Specs)", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Exists so the programmer is not blocked waiting on final art and the designer is not guessing at dimensions. Placeholders and final art use the exact same file path, so swapping is a file replacement rather than a code change.", "source_file": "Cyber_Wellness_Quest_Milestones.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "cyber_wellness_quest_milestones_art_manifest", "label": "ART_MANIFEST Texture Declaration", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Chosen over flat-colour placeholder image files because it hands the designer a named, measured shopping list (15 textures with filenames, frame sizes and counts, plus ART_ANIMS) instead of rectangles to reverse-engineer, and keeps the scene code art-agnostic. Its measured sizes supersede the spec table's guessed 64x64, which was invented before the 1120x280 level existed.", "source_file": "Cyber_Wellness_Quest_Milestones.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "cyber_wellness_quest_milestones_skin_system", "label": "Skin-Based Art Swap-In (SKINS / ACTIVE_SKIN)", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "A skin declares only the textures it actually replaces and carries its own frame sizes, animation frame lists and player hitbox, so a partial art delivery still runs and a missing or corrupt file falls back silently to the procedural version instead of crashing.", "source_file": "Cyber_Wellness_Quest_Milestones.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "cyber_wellness_quest_milestones_brackeys_cc0_skin", "label": "Brackeys CC0 Placeholder Skin", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "ACTIVE_SKIN = 'brackeys' maps the traveler to knight.png and the hacker to slime_purple.png. Deliberately pixel art, not the game's flat vector style - it proves the swap path works but must be replaced.", "source_file": "Cyber_Wellness_Quest_Milestones.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "cyber_wellness_quest_milestones_no_godot_decision", "label": "No Godot - Stay on React/Vite", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "The Godot port was dropped with no code written against it. A single web codebase avoids a second toolchain and keeps the zero-install browser deployment; a Godot HTML5 export would add a WASM runtime, the wrong trade for load time on older school devices.", "source_file": "Cyber_Wellness_Quest_Milestones.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "cyber_wellness_quest_milestones_phaser_scoped_lazy_load", "label": "Phaser Scoped to Two Mechanics, Lazy-Loaded", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Phaser is used only for the Platformer and stepping-stone run, for its physics/animation tooling; every other mechanic stays plain React because the existing pattern already works. It loads only when a P4-P6 player enters Passworld or Privacy Peaks, so the hub, the other realms and the whole P1-P3 path never pay for it (~1.48MB chunk vs a ~248KB main bundle).", "source_file": "Cyber_Wellness_Quest_Milestones.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "cyber_wellness_quest_milestones_phaser_minigame_wrapper", "label": "PhaserMiniGame Wrapper", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Mounts and unmounts a Phaser canvas inside a React container and cleans up on unmount. Extended to accept a (Phaser) => config factory, because a Scene class must extend Phaser.Scene and cannot be defined until the dynamic import resolves.", "source_file": "Cyber_Wellness_Quest_Milestones.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "cyber_wellness_quest_milestones_platformer_mechanic", "label": "Platformer Mechanic (Guard the Vault: Level Up)", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Passworld P4-P6, reworked into one continuous 3144px scrollable Phaser level in five movements so story, the Sam & Tom decision and the vault challenge all live inside the scene, gated by a portcullis rather than a DOM panel. Six characters to collect because a strong password is a long one; all 19 jumps verified against the physics rather than eyeballed; guards snapped onto their platforms with 190px ledges and a 440px/s knockback.", "source_file": "Cyber_Wellness_Quest_Milestones.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "cyber_wellness_quest_milestones_stepping_stones_mechanic", "label": "Stepping-Stone Decision Run", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Privacy Peaks P4-P6. Six stones presented one at a time with Step-on-it/Skip-it; decision logic stays in React (same pattern as MiniGameSpot) and Phaser is purely the visual run of stones, fog and the Traveler hop. Still has no ART_MANIFEST/skin treatment.", "source_file": "Cyber_Wellness_Quest_Milestones.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "cyber_wellness_quest_milestones_compare_mechanic", "label": "Detective/Compare Mechanic (MiniGameCompare)", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Unblocked by dropping the assumption that 'Compare' means two photographs - the comparison that carries a media-literacy lesson is the trusted original against the version going around, which is text and chrome, so it needed no art and was never actually blocked. One component serves both bands via a framework field ('stopcheck' for P1-P3, 'sure' for P4-P6); controls are Sort's and Spot's, and only an exact match completes it. Replaced the Spot/Sort stand-ins in Fable Falls.", "source_file": "Cyber_Wellness_Quest_Milestones.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "cyber_wellness_quest_milestones_judgement_design_rule", "label": "A Mini-Game Must Not Be Passable Without Judgement", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "An audit found four of five mini-games could be finished without deciding anything, so they looked like they taught judgement while rewarding exhaustive clicking - exactly the habit these lessons exist to counter. All four now require the judgement to be right, with free retries and no fail state: the fix is never punishment, it is removing the path that skipped the thinking. Balance Bay is deliberately excepted because it is a values exercise with no correct answer, so gating it would misrepresent what it teaches.", "source_file": "Cyber_Wellness_Quest_Milestones.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "cyber_wellness_quest_milestones_vault_door_gate", "label": "Vault Door Judgement Gate", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Everything collected goes into a bag, weak pieces included, and a locked vault door on the final platform asks which of them belong in a strong password. Two gates: it refuses outright if the strong pieces are not all there, and otherwise the player must pick them out from the decoys they also carried up. Decoys had to become collectable for this to mean anything.", "source_file": "Cyber_Wellness_Quest_Milestones.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "cyber_wellness_quest_milestones_removed_visual_tells", "label": "Removed Visual Tells", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Five tells gave the answer away before the student read a word: closed vs open padlocks on tile art, gold gloss and sparkles on decoys, real tiles hovering while decoys glinted, a HUD reading 'n of 6 strong', and a strength meter that filled only on real pickups and ran red-to-teal. Two had been explicitly requested by the designer brief, now corrected there. One uniform collectible design is a hard constraint, not a preference.", "source_file": "Cyber_Wellness_Quest_Milestones.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "cyber_wellness_quest_milestones_input_scope_decision", "label": "Input Scope: Keyboard + Mouse Only", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Decided 19 Aug 2026. Touch/tablet parity is explicitly not a goal; the on-screen d-pad, tap-to-move, drag-to-steer and 48px tap-target items were dropped rather than deferred. This closes the former keyboard-only 'blocker' - WASD/arrows to walk and Space/Enter to interact are the intended primary input, not a regression.", "source_file": "Cyber_Wellness_Quest_Milestones.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "cyber_wellness_quest_milestones_band_select_atlas_gate", "label": "Band Select in the Atlas Gate", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "A routing/state decision inside the existing gate flow, not a second app shell. Restaged 18-19 Aug 2026 as a panel over the Traveler's Room rather than a bare card screen, so what needs designing is the panel chrome, not a full screen.", "source_file": "Cyber_Wellness_Quest_Milestones.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "cyber_wellness_quest_milestones_travelers_room_prologue", "label": "The Traveler's Room Prologue", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "The game opens in the Traveler's bedroom instead of a card screen: walk to a glowing diary, Comet unfolds out of it, naming and band-select run as a panel over the room, then the door leads out to the Atlas. Built on the existing World/useWalker layer so it inherited hotspots, objectives and pausing for free. Ships third-party pixel art in an otherwise flat-vector game - a style call nobody has made yet, on the first screen every student sees.", "source_file": "Cyber_Wellness_Quest_Milestones.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "cyber_wellness_quest_milestones_hub_order_disagreement", "label": "Hub Order Doc Disagreement", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "HUB_ORDER is still keyed by band but both keys point at one array taken from storyline.md's Story Arc Overview, while Improvement Plan section 4 still specifies two different per-band orders. Reinstating a split is a one-line change; the open decision is which doc wins.", "source_file": "Cyber_Wellness_Quest_Milestones.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "cyber_wellness_quest_milestones_session_persistence", "label": "Session Persistence (localStorage)", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Not a gap - travelerName, band, realmProgress and pledgeSigned have persisted to localStorage under 'cyber-wellness-quest/v1' since before this project's phases began, so the self-directed-over-the-holidays scenario is already covered.", "source_file": "Cyber_Wellness_Quest_Milestones.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "cyber_wellness_quest_milestones_report_block_component", "label": "ReportBlock Component", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "The reusable Report & Block resolution, wired into the redirect moment in every realm.", "source_file": "Cyber_Wellness_Quest_Milestones.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "cyber_wellness_quest_milestones_realm_content_schema", "label": "Per-Band Realm Content Schema", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "realms.js restructured to bands: { lower, higher } per realm with getBandView() resolution and a null-band fallback to lower, plus ACTIVE_REALMS filtering disabled realms so every consumer reads the realm count from the schema instead of hardcoding four. Band objects swap wholesale rather than per-field, so a band needing its own extraBeats carries them itself.", "source_file": "Cyber_Wellness_Quest_Milestones.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "cyber_wellness_quest_milestones_branching_atlas_map", "label": "Branching Atlas Map", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "The hub's single winding stream became 5 branches fanning out from the Gate, one per realm, so any hub art must be drawn against the new layout. The Atlas also now remembers where the Traveler left the boat via atlasPos rather than returning them to the Gate.", "source_file": "Cyber_Wellness_Quest_Milestones.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "cyber_wellness_quest_milestones_fixed_viewport_layout", "label": "Fixed Viewport, No Page Scrolling", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "A 2:1 scene box wide enough to play is half the viewport tall on its own, so stacking it in one column made every screen scroll. Screens with content below the box now use a two-column stage that restacks under 900px, and the box takes its height from its container and derives width via aspect-ratio - sizing it as a share of the viewport cannot work because the chrome above it differs per screen.", "source_file": "Cyber_Wellness_Quest_Milestones.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "cyber_wellness_quest_milestones_font_subset_trim", "label": "Latin-Only Font Subsets", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "The bare @fontsource weight entrypoints shipped devanagari, vietnamese and cyrillic subsets - 76% of a 1023KB payload for a game with no text in those scripts. unicode-range meant browsers never downloaded them, so this is a deploy-size win rather than a first-paint one, but it matters for the older-school-devices constraint.", "source_file": "Cyber_Wellness_Quest_Milestones.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "cyber_wellness_quest_milestones_accessibility_audit_gap", "label": "Reduced-Motion Coverage Gap", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "The prefers-reduced-motion block only blankets CSS animation and transition; the Phaser tweens (guard patrols, tile hover, vault door, win sequence) and the rAF walker are JS-driven and ignore it entirely.", "source_file": "Cyber_Wellness_Quest_Milestones.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "cyber_wellness_quest_milestones_phase_0_foundation", "target": "cyber_wellness_quest_milestones_realm_content_schema", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "Cyber_Wellness_Quest_Milestones.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "cyber_wellness_quest_milestones_phase_0_foundation", "target": "cyber_wellness_quest_milestones_band_select_atlas_gate", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "Cyber_Wellness_Quest_Milestones.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "cyber_wellness_quest_milestones_phase_0_foundation", "target": "cyber_wellness_quest_milestones_phaser_minigame_wrapper", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "Cyber_Wellness_Quest_Milestones.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "cyber_wellness_quest_milestones_phase_0_foundation", "target": "cyber_wellness_quest_milestones_asset_pipeline", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "Cyber_Wellness_Quest_Milestones.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "cyber_wellness_quest_milestones_phase_0_foundation", "target": "design_component_inventory", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "Cyber_Wellness_Quest_Milestones.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "cyber_wellness_quest_milestones_phase_1_content_authoring", "target": "cyber_wellness_quest_milestones_report_block_component", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "Cyber_Wellness_Quest_Milestones.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "cyber_wellness_quest_milestones_phase_1_content_authoring", "target": "cyber_wellness_quest_improvement_plan_fifth_pledge_line", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "Cyber_Wellness_Quest_Milestones.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "cyber_wellness_quest_milestones_phase_1_content_authoring", "target": "cyber_wellness_quest_improvement_plan_fable_falls", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "Cyber_Wellness_Quest_Milestones.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "cyber_wellness_quest_milestones_phase_1_content_authoring", "target": "cyber_wellness_quest_improvement_plan_digital_footprint_gap", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "Cyber_Wellness_Quest_Milestones.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "cyber_wellness_quest_milestones_phase_2_new_mechanics", "target": "cyber_wellness_quest_milestones_platformer_mechanic", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "Cyber_Wellness_Quest_Milestones.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "cyber_wellness_quest_milestones_phase_2_new_mechanics", "target": "cyber_wellness_quest_milestones_stepping_stones_mechanic", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "Cyber_Wellness_Quest_Milestones.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "cyber_wellness_quest_milestones_phase_2_new_mechanics", "target": "cyber_wellness_quest_milestones_compare_mechanic", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "Cyber_Wellness_Quest_Milestones.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "cyber_wellness_quest_milestones_phase_2_new_mechanics", "target": "cyber_wellness_quest_milestones_judgement_design_rule", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "Cyber_Wellness_Quest_Milestones.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "cyber_wellness_quest_milestones_phase_3_backgrounds", "target": "cyber_wellness_quest_milestones_travelers_room_prologue", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "Cyber_Wellness_Quest_Milestones.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "cyber_wellness